    O6  Inspection, artifacts, and CLI public boundary
        - Pure graph/transition functions consume inert definitions/snapshots. Live inspection
          consumes committed private TurnRecord/LifecycleRecord data; inspect owns private v2
          codecs/artifacts. Sink attachment returns { drain, dispose }; buffer sinks have explicit
          capacity; artifact bytes use one file-neutral defensive-copy carrier. There is no second
          mutable history or fabricated trace from arbitrary snapshots. Planner output may show
          selection, microsteps, memory patches, desired plans, but not actual
          starts/releases/generations/pending outcomes/finalizers. TurnRecord is private and
          projections are inferred. Slow sinks cannot delay ack/StoreFanout; a failed sink detaches
          while others continue. Import/export never exposes private v2 model, TurnRecords, runtime
          ownership, or raw Cause. One formatter exists per projection; attachment observes records
          admitted after attach. Only route-created sinks and validated inferred projections are
          accepted; retention is bounded; caller mutation of bytes cannot mutate artifacts.

        - The existing exportTraceArtifact route accepts an optional redaction policy.
          ArtifactExportOptions has optional redactions: a list of { path: ArtifactValuePath,
          replacement: "[REDACTED]" }. ArtifactCanonicalPath is (string | number)[].
        - ArtifactValuePath alternatives:
          - `["records", number, "snapshot", "memory" | "context", ...ArtifactCanonicalPath]`
          - `["records", number, "facts", number, "data" | "value" | "error" | "defect" | "latest",
            ...ArtifactCanonicalPath]`
          - `["checkpoints", number, "actors", number, "snapshot", "memory" | "context",
            ...ArtifactCanonicalPath]`
          - `["checkpoints", number, "snapshot", "memory" | "context", ...ArtifactCanonicalPath]`

        - exportTraceArtifact accepts ReturnType<typeof importTraceArtifact> and optional
          ArtifactExportOptions. It returns Uint8Array.

        - Redaction is explicit, pure, and applied to a defensive export projection. Omitted/empty
          policy returns a byte-identical importable raw artifact. Non-empty policy emits only the
          export-only share projection defined by @plan.Artifacts.O6. Replace only application-owned
          carriers at named paths with the fixed string. Never target identity, AppPlan fingerprint,
          version, discriminants, ordering, sequence, truncation, diagnostic codes, cleanup/status
          structure. Paths follow the share-projection rules in @plan.Artifacts.O6.
          Array indexes must be exact and non-negative; wildcards are forbidden.
          Paths must exist; duplicate or ancestor/descendant overlap rejects as
          InvalidArtifactOperand.
          Never mutate runtime,
          persistence, or decoded models; share output is not boot/persistence input and
          importTraceArtifact rejects it as WrongArtifactKind. Runtime, persisted record, raw
          artifact, and canonical evidence remain unchanged.

        - The installed flow-state binary follows CLI.md for exact grammar and typed gateway.
        - It preserves bounded v2 artifacts and Story-executor parity.
        - It preserves envelopes, stdout/stderr, exit/signal, atomic files, and truncation.
        - behavior check is the only new leaf beyond retained behavior/Story/trace families.
          Model paths are programmatic. Schemas represent app Stories, exact actor
          evidence, run.end, module ownership, compound states, context requirements, lifecycle
          records, and operation identities before promotion. Accept only registered behavior and
          typed artifacts; reject arbitrary payload-bearing event JSON, old Scenario/local-proof
          compatibility input, batch Story execution, or another history/runner owner.

        - Redaction is a vNext additive amendment. Raw runtime truth and the default export remain
          unchanged. @plan.Artifacts.O6 owns raw importable artifacts and the export-only share
          projection. @plan.CLI.O1 and @plan.CLI.O2 own exact CLI grammar. Inspection, redaction,
          and CLI examples appear below. CONTRACT.md §§1-3 add no CLI/artifact authority. Runtime
          artifact and read boundaries belong to @plan.RuntimeV2.O5.
        - @O6 owns the redaction signature; AMEND-API-003 is its source trace.
          @plan.Artifacts.O6 owns its wire schema and behavior.


        Example:
        ```ts
        const attachment = attachInspectionSink(runtime, sink);
        await attachment.drain();
        const bytes = new Uint8Array(); // illustrative artifact input
        const trace = importTraceArtifact(bytes);
        const artifact = exportTraceArtifact(trace);
        ```
        Example:
        ```ts
        type ArtifactExportOptions = {
          redactions?: {
            path: ArtifactValuePath;
            replacement: "[REDACTED]";
          }[];
        };

        type ArtifactCanonicalPath = (string | number)[];
        type ArtifactValuePath =
          | ["records", number, "snapshot", "memory" | "context", ...ArtifactCanonicalPath]
          | [
              "records",
              number,
              "facts",
              number,
              "data" | "value" | "error" | "defect" | "latest",
              ...ArtifactCanonicalPath,
            ]
          | [
              "checkpoints",
              number,
              "actors",
              number,
              "snapshot",
              "memory" | "context",
              ...ArtifactCanonicalPath,
            ]
          | ["checkpoints", number, "snapshot", "memory" | "context", ...ArtifactCanonicalPath];

        declare function exportTraceArtifact(
          trace: ReturnType<typeof importTraceArtifact>,
          options?: ArtifactExportOptions,
        ): Uint8Array;
        ```
        Example:
        ```ts
        const command: "flow-state behavior check" = "flow-state behavior check";
        ```
decisions
    D1  Isolated named route ownership
        Each package route is a named-export surface with local consumer aliases.
        Root Implementation has only the succeed/effect/merge value members and
        is not a package namespace. Non-root routes do not re-export root
        builders.

    D2  Preserve current target disposition
        Apply the temporary export and ownerless-name dispositions in @O1.
        Retain future shapes and proof obligations without claiming implementation.
        The additive quickstart reaches temporary
        readiness; its actor continuation remains a commented future target.

constraints
    C1  Plan ownership boundaries
        - This Plan owns the public consumer shape. Inference and variance belong to @plan.Types.O1
          and @plan.Types.O2; diagnostics belong to @plan.DiagnosticsV2.O1, @plan.DiagnosticsV2.O2, and
          @plan.DiagnosticsV2.O3. Runtime terminology, identity, and lifecycle belong to
          @plan.RuntimeV2.O1, @plan.RuntimeV2.O3, and @plan.RuntimeV2.O4. Do not duplicate or widen those
          Plan requirements.

    C2  No new public alternatives
        - Do not add namespace objects, private deep-import routes, aliases, or generic operation
          refs/registries.
          Do not add child-machine/dynamic actor categories or registered views.
          Do not add testing/inspection artifact hierarchies, arbitrary event-payload CLI input,
          or uncontracted runner/host surfaces.

verification
    V1  Route and declaration surface
        - Outcome: @O1.

        - Scenario: inspect public declarations and packed package exports.

        - Pass when active root names and value/type duals match @O1.
          Deferred names remain absent until owners/proofs land.
          The three non-root route modules have the authorized current disposition.
          Prohibited namespace/deep imports are absent.

        - Check path: nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types; nub run --filter
          flow-state-rewrite check:packed-consumers;
          packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/public/test/public-routes.test.ts.

        - Pending gap: these checks must assert the complete active/future route lists and negative
          names; Plan creation does not prove that assertion.

    V2  Authoring and behavior grammar
        - Outcome: @O2.

        - Scenario: compile valid recursive definitions/machines and reject invalid
          state/event/configuration shapes; exercise callback failure boundaries and an aborting
          macrostep.

        - Pass when depth ten is accepted and depth eleven rejects synchronously.
          Exact tokens and narrowing hold. The exact grammar and selector rules apply.
          Malformed callbacks/config defects publish no state and start no work.
          All failures have canonical Diagnostic behavior.

        - Check path: nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types; nub run test --
          packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/definition/test/definition.test.ts
          packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/machine/test/machine.test.ts.

        - Pending gap: target-contract runtime macrostep/selector proof coverage is not established
          by those paths alone.

    V3  Resource keys and family behavior
        - Outcome: @O3.

        - Scenario: check exact generic methods/state unions, canonical byte/path behavior,
          invalidation/clear bounds, and resource/transaction/stream lifetime outcomes.

        - Pass when every state discriminant/field and P/K/A/E/V/R relation is exact.
          Canonical K enforces the 16/256/8192 limits and grammar.
          Invalid input has no side effects. Occurrence/generation/family rules and exact
          cancellation boundaries hold.

        - Check path: nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types; nub run test --
          packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/operation/test/key.test.ts
          packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/operation/test/operation.test.ts.

        - Pending gap: full production resource/transaction/stream parity and declaration-slot proof
          remain required.

    V4  App, actor, Runtime, and host boundary
        - Outcome: @O4.

        - Scenario: assert exact App.M closure, current shell limitations, actor/ref/lease types,
          runtime lifecycle, passive React reads, and readiness/host behavior.

        - Pass when current RuntimeSetup exposes only app/construct/ready.
          Its providers acquire sequentially, and it caches one terminal Exit.
          Target-only actor/React behaviors are not represented as shipped.
          Target checks match @plan.RuntimeV2.O2, @plan.RuntimeV2.O3, @plan.RuntimeV2.O4, and
          @plan.RuntimeV2.O5.

        - Check path: nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types; nub run --filter
          flow-state-rewrite check:packed-consumers; nub run test --
          packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/app/test/app.test.ts.

        - Pending gap: complete actor, persistence, React 18/19, lifecycle and disposal target
          proofs remain open.

    V5  Story/testing proof surface
        - Outcome: @O5.

        - Scenario: compile positive and negative Story constructors, options, and
          command/checkpoint/run types.
          Run app and machine stories through production bootstrap, cancellation, cleanup, and
          evidence capture.

        - Pass when targets, options, and checkpoint maps remain exact.
          Plan prefixes are immutable, and derived runs are isolated.
          No result injection occurs. Cleanup failure cannot become success.
          Model traversal remains pure.

        - Check path: nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types; nub run test --
          packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/public/test/public-routes.test.ts.

        - Pending gap: Story, gateway, fixture, model, production parity and evidence-sequence
          focused proof files must cover the target contract.

    V6  Inspection, redaction, and CLI
        - Outcome: @O6.

        - Scenario: observe publication through bounded sinks; export/import raw artifacts; export
          with valid and invalid redaction policies; run CLI check through the typed gateway.

        - Pass when omitted/empty policy is byte-identical to the raw artifact.
          Non-empty policy emits only the share projection.
          Policy validation and deterministic manifests hold.
          Source runtime, persistence, and evidence remain unchanged.
          Share output rejects as WrongArtifactKind.
          CLI shares production Story/evidence ownership and rejects arbitrary event fabrication.

        - Check path: nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types; nub run --filter
          flow-state-rewrite check:packed-consumers; nub run test.

        - Pending gap: inspection sink, share redaction, and CLI parity production proofs are not
          established by the generic commands alone.

    V7  Public proof obligations
        - Outcomes: @O1, @O2, @O3, @O4, @O5, @O6.

        - Scenario: run all named proof owners after implementation is complete.

        - Pass when each proof establishes its boundary:
          - Export/deletion proves packed routes and lease boundaries.
          - Grammar proves exact authoring and inference.
          - Production proves runtime behavior without uncontracted API.
          - Artifact proofs cover default-equivalent raw export, redacted share output, path
            validation, determinism, non-mutation, and wrong-kind rejection.

        - Check path: nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types; nub run --filter
          flow-state-rewrite check:packed-consumers; nub run test; nub run --filter
          flow-state-rewrite build.

        - Pending gap: a source-text/type check cannot satisfy runtime proofs; add and run the named
          production behavior proofs before treating any outcome as verified.

        Example: proof-owner index.
        ```ts
        type PublicProof = "API-P01" | "API-P02" | "API-P03" | "API-P04";
        ```

